{{- define "verdict-submission" -}}

--- VERDICT SUBMISSION (MANDATORY - DO NOT SKIP) ---
⚠️  You MUST execute the {{binaryName}} submit-verdict CLI command IN THIS SAME SESSION:
  APPROVED: {{binaryName}} submit-verdict {{.TaskID}} APPROVED --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
  REJECTED (use heredoc to avoid shell quoting issues with markdown):
    reason=$(cat <<'VERDICT'
    <detailed rejection — markdown, backticks, apostrophes all safe here>
    VERDICT
    )
    {{binaryName}} submit-verdict {{.TaskID}} REJECTED --reason "$reason" --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
After APPROVED, exit normally. After REJECTED, follow the
reviewer-state-transitions await-resubmission rules; do not exit while that
non-terminal wait is required.

❌ FAILURE MODE: Completing review, saying "I recommend APPROVED", then exiting WITHOUT running the command.
The CLI command IS the deliverable. Analysis without command execution = nothing happened.
{{- end -}}
